CryoSAGE
========

This source distribution contains Gaussian reconstruction workflows and
state-dependent modeling developed in a local research working tree.
The training package was reorganized for CryoSAGE; it does not require an
installed cryostar package or that project's directory structure.

Adapted components
------------------
Selected experiment initialization, image/STAR handling, Fourier transforms,
translations, CTF model wrappers and geometric utilities were adapted from
CryoSTAR (Yi Zhou, Jing Yuan, Yilai Li and contributors):
https://github.com/bytedance/cryostar
These adaptations retain the Apache-2.0 license. The exact local source files
and their hashes are recorded in provenance.json. The training programs also
include subsequent local Gaussian and occupancy modeling changes.

No GPL-licensed source files were copied into cryosage/utils/optics.py or
cryosage/utils/latent.py. These small modules implement the conventional CTF
equations and public NumPy/SciPy/scikit-learn operations directly. The CTF
polarity convention and posterior-latent analysis are compatible with the
existing workflows. cryoDRGN is a relevant methodological reference:
https://github.com/ml-struct-bio/cryodrgn

